# Local deploy

The agent image copies `app/` and `knowledge/` at build time (`agent/Dockerfile`). Restarting `clinical-companion-agent` keeps the old prompt and the old tool loop.

After changing agent code, from `FinalProject/app`:

```bash
docker compose up -d --build agent
```

A chat that still ends with “general knowledge and not a citation from the book or the web” is the previous image. Confirm the running process with:

```bash
docker exec clinical-companion-agent python -c "import app.internal.graph as g; print(hasattr(g, 'EvidenceMiddleware'))"
```

That print is `True` on the current companion. Weaviate data stays in the `weaviate_data` volume across this rebuild.
